  "description": "The bottom panel's text '49 people were killed at christchurch mosques' is juxtaposed with the visual of a crying man labeled 'muslim'. This mapping implies that the man represents or embodies the emotional reaction to the event described in the text, specifically portraying him as overly emotional or grieving. The text explicitly labels the event, and the visual material (the man) is mapped onto this event through the label 'muslim', creating an analogical mapping where the man is presented as a representative of the Muslim community's supposed reaction to the Christchurch mosque shootings.",
